From: kaiter <kaiter@example.com>
Date: Thu, 14 Nov 2026 03:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Disable U-Boot PCIe training to prevent hang on A7Z

This patch disables PCIe training in U-Boot during the boot stage to prevent
the system from hanging when PCIe2 is misidentified as PCIe3. This is a known
issue in AllWinner BSP where improper PCIe enumeration during U-Boot causes
the boot process to hang indefinitely.

The fix involves:
1. Adding skip-uboot-pcie-training flag in device tree
2. Disabling PCIe initialization code in U-Boot
3. Allowing PCIe to be properly detected in Linux kernel instead

This allows the system to boot successfully even when PCIe devices are present.

Signed-off-by: kaiter <kaiter@example.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7z.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7z.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7z.dts
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7z.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7z.dts
@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@ &pcie_rc {
 	power-gpios =  <&pio PD 20 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	reset-gpios = <&pio PD 22 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	wake-gpios = <&pio PD 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	pcie1v8-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
 	pcie3v3-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
+	/* Disable PCIe training in U-Boot to prevent hang when PCIe2 is misidentified as PCIe3 */
+	skip-uboot-pcie-training = <1>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
